---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Litter Ledger — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 77"
  description="Chullin 77: a placenta is found after slaughter, or a firstborn drops one before anyone sees the lamb. The mishna rules by rov — the majority. Work Rav Ika's own arithmetic yourself: split a herd into buckets, and watch the halakha follow whichever bucket wins."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0b120d] !text-[#e7e4d2]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#24301f] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#131b13]/80 to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#c9a227]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#e0bc3f]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 77 · 2026-07-16
      </p>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">⚖️ The Litter Ledger</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-1 text-xl !text-[#e0bc3f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">סְמוֹךְ מִיעוּטָא דְּנִדְמֶה לְמֶחֱצָה דִּנְקֵבוֹת</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
        A slaughtered ewe turns out to be carrying a placenta. Was there a lamb no one saw? A firstborn
        drops its afterbirth before the birth itself is witnessed — is a hidden, sanctified newborn
        hiding inside it? The mishna never checks. It counts. <strong class="!text-[#e7e4d2]">Jewish law
        follows the majority</strong> — so the whole question becomes: which bucket is the herd really
        in? Rav Ika bar Rav Ami does the arithmetic on <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.77b.12" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#e0bc3f] underline decoration-[#4a5a3a] hover:!text-[#f0d060]">77b</a>.
        Today, you do it with your hands.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Field notes: what came before ============ -->
      <details class="mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#24301f] bg-[#0f1610] p-5">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9a227]">
          field notes — the daf opens mid-argument (77a:1–10) ▾
        </summary>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
          <p>
            The page opens still inside yesterday's sugya: are the sinews on a snapped leg-bone counted
            as covering "flesh"? Rav Pappa corners Rabba with Reish Lakish's stricter view and Rabba goes
            silent — until the Gemara explains that Rabbi Yoḥanan himself backed down:
            <span class="frank !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">״אַל תַּקְנִיטֵנִי, בִּלְשׁוֹן יָחִיד אֲנִי שׁוֹנֶה אוֹתָהּ״</span>
            — <em>"don't provoke me, I teach it as a lone opinion"</em> (77a:4).
          </p>
          <p>
            Then a real case: a bone broke and poked through the skin, with one splinter <em>(kurtita)</em>
            missing. It sat on Abaye's desk for <strong class="!text-[#cfc9a8]">three pilgrimage festivals</strong>
            before he had Sages enough on hand to rule. Rava, whose "knife was sharp," disposed of it in one
            line:
            <span class="frank !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">״מָה לִי נְפַל, מָה לִי אִיתֵיהּ?״</span>
            — <em>what difference does it make if the splinter fell out or stayed put?</em> — either way, if
            flesh still covers most of the bone, the baraita already permits it (77a:5–6, citing 76b).
          </p>
          <p>Ravina wasn't satisfied. He kept pushing on how little "flesh covering the bone" can mean:</p>
          <div id="dilemma-ladder" class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-2 gap-1.5 text-xs sm:grid-cols-4"></div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#7c8770]">
            Only the ring-cut made it to a verdict — the rest stand exactly as Ravina left them,
            <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">אִיבַּעְיָא לְהוּ</span>, open questions on the daf itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- ============ The Mishna ============ -->
      <div class="mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#24301f] bg-[#0f1610] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9a227]">the mishna · חוּלִּין ע״ז א</p>
        <h2 class="frank mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e7e4d2]">Three rulings on a placenta</h2>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#233221] bg-[#0b1109] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0bc3f]">Found after slaughter</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
              A "hearty soul" may eat it. It carries no impurity at all — not food-impurity, not
              carcass-impurity — unless someone actually intends to eat it, which activates food-impurity only.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[10px] !text-[#5f6b55]">Chullin 77a:11</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#233221] bg-[#0b1109] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0bc3f]">Partly emerged first</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
              Forbidden outright — a placenta beginning to emerge is
              <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">סִימָן וָלָד</span>, a sign the fetus's head may
              already have "been born," which the slaughter can no longer permit.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[10px] !text-[#5f6b55]">Chullin 77a:12</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#233221] bg-[#0b1109] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#e0bc3f]">Firstling or hekdesh?</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
              A firstling's placenta: toss it to the dogs. A consecrated animal's: it must be buried.
              Never at a crossroads, never hung on a tree — that's <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">דַּרְכֵי הָאֱמוֹרִי</span>.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[10px] !text-[#5f6b55]">Chullin 77a:13</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ THE SCALE (main game) ============ -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#3a4a2e] bg-[#0f1610] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9a227]">the scale · play it yourself</p>
        <h2 class="frank mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e7e4d2]">Whichever bucket wins, the herd follows</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
          One rule runs the whole mishna: <span class="frank !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">אָזְלִינַן בָּתַר רוּבָּא</span>
          — go after the majority. Sort a hundred births into a bucket that <em>would</em> carry a concern
          and one that wouldn't. Whichever bucket is bigger, that's how the whole herd is treated.
        </p>

        <!-- scenario toggle -->
        <div class="mt-4 flex rounded-xl border border-[#3a4a2e] bg-[#0b1109] p-1" role="group" aria-label="Choose a scenario">
          <button id="btn-bechor" type="button" class="scenario-btn flex-1 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm" aria-pressed="true">
            🐐 A firstling's litter <span class="frank block text-[11px] font-normal opacity-80" dir="rtl" lang="he">בְּכוֹרָה</span>
          </button>
          <button id="btn-hekdesh" type="button" class="scenario-btn flex-1 rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm" aria-pressed="false">
            🕊️ A consecrated mother's litter <span class="frank block text-[11px] font-normal opacity-80" dir="rtl" lang="he">מֻקְדָּשִׁין</span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- bechor slider -->
        <div id="slider-wrap" class="mt-4">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between text-xs">
            <label for="nidmeh" class="!text-[#9aa38c]">
              Your estimate of <span class="frank !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">נִדְמֶה</span> —
              births that resemble a different species
            </label>
            <span id="nidmeh-val" class="font-mono !text-[#e0bc3f]"></span>
          </div>
          <input id="nidmeh" type="range" min="2" max="40" value="15" step="1" class="mt-2 w-full" />
          <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] !text-[#5f6b55]">
            Any number here is a genuine <span class="frank" dir="rtl" lang="he">מִעוּט</span> (minority) —
            the Gemara never puts a figure on it. Slide anywhere in range and watch what happens to the
            bucket below.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p id="hekdesh-note" class="mt-4 hidden text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
          No subtraction trick is needed here. Firstling-sanctity requires a <em>male</em> that also
          <em>matches its mother's species</em> — a narrow slice, small enough to combine into a minority.
          Consecration doesn't care about either: male or female, matching or not, an offspring of a
          dedicated mother can carry her sanctity. Nearly the whole litter counts.
        </p>

        <!-- population grid -->
        <div class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-[#233221] bg-[#0b1109] p-4">
          <div id="grid" class="grid grid-cols-10 gap-[3px]" role="img" aria-label="100 births, split into two buckets"></div>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 text-xs">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="flex items-center gap-1 !text-[#c2694f]"><i class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-sm bg-[#c2694f]"></i> sanctity-risk bucket</span>
              <span class="flex items-center gap-1 !text-[#7fae7a]"><i class="inline-block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-sm bg-[#7fae7a]"></i> no concern</span>
            </div>
            <span id="count-readout" class="font-mono font-bold !text-[#e7e4d2]"></span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- verdict -->
        <div id="verdict" class="mt-4 rounded-xl border p-4"></div>

        <p id="badge-note" class="mt-3 hidden text-center text-xs !text-[#e0bc3f]">
          🏅 You've stress-tested the range, low, middle, and high — Rav Ika's bucket never once flips.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Darkei ha-Emori footnote ============ -->
      <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#24301f] bg-[#0f1610] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c9a227]">one more line, before the burial</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
          Why is burying a placenta at a crossroads, or hanging it on a tree, forbidden as
          <span class="frank !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">דַּרְכֵי הָאֱמוֹרִי</span> — the ways of the
          Amorite — while burying it plainly is not? Abaye and Rava give the rule that decides it, and
          every case after: <span class="frank !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">כׇּל דָּבָר שֶׁיֵּשׁ בּוֹ רְפוּאָה אֵין בּוֹ מִשּׁוּם דַּרְכֵי הָאֱמוֹרִי</span> —
          anything with a real, reasoned purpose behind it is not superstition, even if it looks like it
          (77b:15). The Gemara immediately tests the rule on a tree that keeps shedding its fruit — red
          paint and a load of stones — and the argument is still running when this side of the daf ends
          (77b:16). It's picked back up, and resolved, on the next daf: the <a href="/daf/chullin-78" class="!text-[#c9b891] underline decoration-[#4a5a3a] hover:!text-[#e0bc3f]">Sealed Dockets</a> game.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-[#24301f] pt-8">
        <h3 class="frank mb-3 text-xl font-bold !text-[#c9a227]">Learn the real daf</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#9aa38c]">
          Chullin 77 closes out the sinews-and-tereifa sugya that began the day before, then opens a new
          mishna on placentas found inside a slaughtered animal. The Gemara traces every ruling to its
          root: a verse (Deuteronomy 14:6) that includes the placenta in "you may eat," a dispute between
          Rabbi Elazar and Rabbi Yoḥanan over whether a placenta found alongside an actual fetus still
          carries the concern for a second, unseen one, and finally Rav Ika bar Rav Ami's rov/miut
          arithmetic — the same move this page hands you the controls for.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-xs">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.77a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a4a2e] bg-[#131b13]/60 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#c9a227] hover:border-[#c9a227]">Chullin 77 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#24301f] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9aa38c]">Rashi ×75</span>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#24301f] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9aa38c]">Steinsaltz ×32</span>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#24301f] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9aa38c]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×20</span>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#24301f] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#9aa38c]">Tosafot ×11</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-xs !text-[#5f6b55]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#3a4a2e] hover:!text-[#9aa38c]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a> —
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank {
      font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    }

    .scenario-btn {
      color: #8a967c;
      transition: background-color 0.15s, color 0.15s;
    }
    .scenario-btn:hover { color: #cfc9a8; }
    .scenario-btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #c9a227; outline-offset: -2px; }
    .scenario-btn[aria-pressed='true'] {
      background: #c9a227;
      color: #0b1109 !important;
    }

    #grid > div {
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
      border-radius: 2px;
      transition: background-color 0.45s ease;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      #grid > div { transition: none; }
    }

    input[type='range'] {
      -webkit-appearance: none;
      appearance: none;
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, #7fae7a, #c9a227 50%, #c2694f);
      outline: none;
    }
    input[type='range']::-webkit-slider-thumb {
      -webkit-appearance: none;
      appearance: none;
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: #e7e4d2;
      border: 2px solid #0b1109;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    input[type='range']::-moz-range-thumb {
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: #e7e4d2;
      border: 2px solid #0b1109;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .ladder-card {
      border: 1px solid #233221;
      border-radius: 0.6rem;
      background: #0b1109;
      padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;

    // ---------- Field notes: Ravina's escalating dilemma (77a:7–10) ----------
    const LADDER = [
      { he: 'מִתְלַקֵּט', en: 'gathered', open: true },
      { he: 'מִתְרוֹסֵס', en: 'pulverized', open: true },
      { he: 'מִתְמַסְמֵס', en: 'decomposed', open: true },
      { he: 'נִיקַּב', en: 'perforated', open: true },
      { he: 'נִקְלַף', en: 'peeled', open: true },
      { he: 'נִסְדַּק', en: 'cracked', open: true },
      { he: 'שְׁלִישׁ הַתַּחְתּוֹן נִיטַּל', en: 'bottom third gone', open: true },
      { he: 'נִקְדַּר כְּמִין טַבַּעַת', en: 'cut in a ring', open: false },
    ];
    $('dilemma-ladder').innerHTML = LADDER.map((d) => `
      <div class="ladder-card">
        <p class="frank text-sm !text-[#cfc9a8]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${d.he}</p>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider ${d.open ? '!text-[#c2694f]' : '!text-[#7fae7a]'}">
          ${d.open ? 'open question' : 'resolved · permitted'}
        </p>
      </div>`).join('');

    // ---------- The Scale ----------
    const TOTAL = 100;
    let scenario: 'bechor' | 'hekdesh' = 'bechor';
    const visited = new Set<string>(); // low/mid/high thirds visited, for the badge
    let badgeShown = false;

    const gridEl = $('grid');
    for (let i = 0; i < TOTAL; i++) {
      const cell = document.createElement('div');
      cell.dataset.idx = String(i);
      gridEl.appendChild(cell);
    }
    const cells = Array.from(gridEl.children) as HTMLElement[];

    function paintGrid(riskCount: number) {
      cells.forEach((cell, i) => {
        cell.style.backgroundColor = i < riskCount ? '#c2694f' : '#7fae7a';
      });
    }

    function renderVerdict(riskCount: number) {
      const majority = riskCount > TOTAL / 2;
      const readout = $('count-readout');
      readout.textContent = `${riskCount} / ${TOTAL}`;
      readout.className = `font-mono font-bold ${majority ? '!text-[#c2694f]' : '!text-[#7fae7a]'}`;

      const verdict = $('verdict');
      if (scenario === 'bechor') {
        verdict.className = 'mt-4 rounded-xl border p-4 border-[#3a5a34] bg-[#0f1a10]';
        verdict.innerHTML = `
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#7fae7a]">${riskCount}/100 → מִעוּט (minority) → no concern</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#c9c4a8]">
            Combine the minority who resemble another species with the half of every litter that's
            female, and the true risk — a matching-species <em>male</em> — is left a minority on its
            own (77b:12–13). <span class="frank !text-[#e0bc3f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">יַשְׁלִיכֶנָּה לַכְּלָבִים</span>
            — cast the placenta to the dogs.
          </p>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.77a.13" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="mt-2 inline-block text-xs !text-[#7fae7a] hover:!text-[#a8cf9a] hover:underline">Chullin 77a:13 ↗</a>`;
      } else {
        verdict.className = 'mt-4 rounded-xl border p-4 border-[#5a3a2e] bg-[#1a0f0c]';
        verdict.innerHTML = `
          <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider !text-[#c2694f]">${riskCount}/100 (illustrative) → רוֹב (majority) → concern stands</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#c9c4a8]">
            <span class="frank !text-[#e0bc3f]" dir="rtl" lang="he">רוּבָּא בַּר מִיקְדָּשׁ הוּא</span> —
            the majority of a consecrated mother's offspring, of either sex, are fit to carry her
            sanctity (77b:14). The placenta must be buried — never at a crossroads, never on a tree.
          </p>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.77a.13" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="mt-2 inline-block text-xs !text-[#c2694f] hover:!text-[#e08a70] hover:underline">Chullin 77a:13 ↗</a>`;
      }
    }

    function thirdOf(n: number) {
      if (n <= 15) return 'low';
      if (n <= 28) return 'mid';
      return 'high';
    }

    function update() {
      let riskCount: number;
      if (scenario === 'bechor') {
        const nidmeh = Number(($('nidmeh') as HTMLInputElement).value);
        $('nidmeh-val').textContent = `${nidmeh}%`;
        riskCount = 50 - nidmeh;
        visited.add(thirdOf(nidmeh));
        if (!badgeShown && visited.has('low') && visited.has('mid') && visited.has('high')) {
          badgeShown = true;
          $('badge-note').classList.remove('hidden');
        }
      } else {
        riskCount = 88;
      }
      paintGrid(riskCount);
      renderVerdict(riskCount);
    }

    function setScenario(next: 'bechor' | 'hekdesh') {
      scenario = next;
      $('btn-bechor').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(next === 'bechor'));
      $('btn-hekdesh').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(next === 'hekdesh'));
      $('slider-wrap').classList.toggle('hidden', next !== 'bechor');
      $('hekdesh-note').classList.toggle('hidden', next !== 'hekdesh');
      update();
    }

    $('btn-bechor').addEventListener('click', () => setScenario('bechor'));
    $('btn-hekdesh').addEventListener('click', () => setScenario('hekdesh'));
    ($('nidmeh') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('input', update);

    setScenario('bechor');
  </script>
</Layout>
